		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=22105#p22105"><![CDATA[
Project Aedra is a free and open-source reimplementation of the engine used in The Elder Scrolls 3: Morrowind. You can check out videos of Project Aedra here:<br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/user/DragonGeo2" class="postlink">http://www.youtube.com/user/DragonGeo2</a><br><br>As always, you can download the source code and precompiled binaries for Project Aedra at the main Sourceforge project page here:<br><a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/aedra/" class="postlink">https://sourceforge.net/projects/aedra/</a><br><br>Versions of Project Aedra prior to r110 use purely raycasted collision detection without Bullet. Versions r110 and greater use *a modified version of* Bullet Collision and Linear Math.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7539">DragonGeo2</a> — Mon Feb 14, 2011 4:10 pm</p><hr />
